# Environment variables for the debridgers-marketing application.
#
# VITE_API_URL, NODE_ENV and PORT live in .env.development.example,
# .env.staging.example and .env.production.example instead of here. Vite
# loads the plain .env file for every mode in addition to the mode-specific
# one, and a key set in .env is NOT overridden by the same key in
# .env.[mode] - it wins regardless of mode. A VITE_API_URL here would
# silently defeat all three mode files at once. Nothing mode-independent
# needs a value yet, so this file is otherwise empty; add a key here only if
# it is genuinely meant to be identical across development, staging and
# production.

# VITE_REQUEST_KEY, VITE_PAYMENT_KEY_1 and VITE_PAYMENT_KEY_2 were removed on
# 2026-08-09. Vite inlines every VITE_ variable into the bundle at build time,
# so they were public strings, not secrets, and the guards reading them have
# been replaced by JWT plus role checks. Do not reintroduce a shared secret that
# the browser has to send; it cannot be kept secret there.
